# Keep host build output out of every image's build context.
#
# The web image installs its dependencies with `npm ci` and then copies the web source over the
# top. Without these lines that copy carries the host's own node_modules in with it, replacing the
# freshly installed Linux packages with whatever the laptop last installed — macOS native bindings
# included. The image then depends on the state of the developer's checkout rather than on the
# lock, and works only while the two happen to agree. When they drifted, the build failed inside
# the bundler with a JavaScript layer from one version calling native code from another.
#
# Scoped to exactly that. The Python images copy named paths and never read anything under web/,
# so these entries cannot change what they contain.
web/node_modules
web/dist
